    {
      "id": "be-s12m-shutdown-long-run-c1",
      "heading": "Losses and the shutdown rule",
      "explanation_md": "Sometimes the price falls below **ATC\\**: the firm makes a **loss\\**. Should it close?\n\nIf it closes, it still has to pay its **fixed costs\\** (rent, machines), so it loses all of them. If it keeps operating and the price covers its **variable costs\\**, every unit also chips in a little towards the fixed costs. So operating loses **less\\**.\n\n**The rule:**\n\n- **Keep operating\\** while **P ≥ min AVC\\**.\n- **Shut down\\** when **P < min AVC\\**.\n\nThat is why the firm's **short-run supply curve\\** is just its **MC curve above minimum AVC\\**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Shut down if P < min AVC; supply curve = MC above min AVC.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
