    {
      "id": "be-s12m-shutdown-long-run-c2",
      "heading": "Market supply",
      "explanation_md": "Pick a price. Ask each firm how much it would supply at that price, and **add the quantities\\**. Do that at every price and you get the **market supply curve\\**.\n\nBecause you add quantities sideways at the same price, this is a **horizontal sum\\**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Market supply = horizontal sum of the firms' supply curves.",
      "clarification": null,
