    {
      "id": "be-s12m-shutdown-long-run-c3",
      "heading": "Entry in the long run",
      "explanation_md": "If firms are making profit and anyone can enter, new firms **pour in\\**. This chain follows:\n\n1. Entry **shifts market supply right\\** (S to S\\*).\n2. The **market price falls\\** (Pe to Pe\\*).\n3. Each firm's flat demand line **drops\\** (Df to Df\\*).\n4. Each firm **cuts output\\** to where the new price meets MC.\n5. Entry stops only when **profit is zero\\**.\n\nAt that point three things are true: **P = MC\\** (socially efficient output), **P = minimum AC\\** (efficient plant size) and **zero profit\\** (firms earn just enough to cover their opportunity cost).\n\nIf there are **barriers to entry\\**, this never happens and profits **persist\\**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Profits attract entry, price falls, profits go to zero; long run: P = MC = minimum AC.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
